# GeoVista configuration.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in what you want. Every key here is OPTIONAL —
# the app runs fully without any of them, using only free, keyless sources:
#
#   Terrain    AWS Terrain Tiles (Terrarium)          no key
#   Imagery    Esri World Imagery                     no key
#   Buildings  OpenStreetMap via Overpass             no key
#   Roads      OpenStreetMap via Overpass             no key
#   Trees      OpenStreetMap via Overpass             no key
#   Geology    Macrostrat                             no key
#
# The keys below swap in higher-fidelity commercial sources on the Globe view.
# `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` values are inlined at build time — rebuild after changing them.

# Cesium Ion — Cesium World Terrain (30 m global DEM with normals and a water
# mask) and Cesium OSM Buildings (global, pre-tiled). Without it the Globe
# falls back to the same free AWS terrain the Terrain view uses, and builds
# buildings from OSM footprints for the selected region.
# Free tier: https://ion.cesium.com/tokens
NEXT_PUBLIC_CESIUM_ION_TOKEN=

# Google Maps Platform key with the **Map Tiles API** enabled — unlocks Google
# Photorealistic 3D Tiles (real mesh capture: buildings, trees, terrain).
# Without it the Photorealistic source is disabled and the Globe uses the
# Cesium/OSM source instead.
# https://console.cloud.google.com/ → APIs & Services → enable "Map Tiles API"
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
